    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty broad list. I'm specifically trying to figure out how to handle variables that might be legally tricky to use directly, like race or ethnicity, since we have to avoid explicit discriminatory modeling. If we can't use race as a feature, what are the best proxy variables that would capture that same neighborhood-level risk profile? I want to make sure the model can still differentiate between high-risk and low-risk areas effectively.",
